1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:12,438
Health Copilot. Your health, organised — your questions, answered. This is a demo of the patient app and the separate practice portal for doctors.

2
00:00:12,888 --> 00:00:32,749
Everything begins with a secure sign-in, backed by real Firebase authentication. Each account is locked to one role — patient or doctor. Notice the language picker in the corner: the whole app is available in English, Hindi, Telugu and Tamil, even before you sign in.

3
00:00:33,199 --> 00:00:44,482
I'll sign in as the built-in sample patient, Alex Morgan. Sample accounts come pre-filled with fictional data, so you can explore everything instantly.

4
00:00:44,932 --> 00:00:53,389
This is the patient dashboard — a calm overview of today's medicines, upcoming appointments, and the latest health trends.

5
00:00:53,839 --> 00:01:15,171
The A.I. Health Assistant is the heart of the app. You can type, speak your question with your voice, or attach a photo. Here I've asked about a headache, and the assistant replies with plain-language, source-linked education. It never diagnoses, and in an emergency it escalates straight away.

6
00:01:15,621 --> 00:01:26,818
Medical Records keep documents in one private library — searchable, filterable, and shared with the care team for review. Uploads store metadata only.

7
00:01:27,268 --> 00:01:34,576
Prescriptions written by the doctor appear in the patient's own list, with a simple daily 'taken' toggle.

8
00:01:35,026 --> 00:01:43,939
Appointments lay out upcoming visits and history on a clear timeline, and let patients apply to doctors in the practice directory.

9
00:01:44,389 --> 00:01:52,442
Health Analytics turns readings into trends over time, with summary cards that compare this period with the last.

10
00:01:52,892 --> 00:01:58,331
Wellness and Goals tracks personal targets and simple daily habits.

11
00:01:58,781 --> 00:02:06,819
Under Settings you control appearance, notifications and privacy — and pick the language for the entire app.

12
00:02:07,269 --> 00:02:12,552
Here is the patient dashboard in English, the default language.

13
00:02:13,002 --> 00:02:20,761
Change the language, and every menu, label and heading updates instantly — here it is in Hindi.

14
00:02:21,211 --> 00:02:31,979
And the very same screen in Telugu. English, Hindi, Telugu and Tamil are all built in, and your choice is remembered for that browser.

15
00:02:32,429 --> 00:02:41,726
Help and Support answers common questions and opens a feedback form with a shared ratings board — available to both patients and doctors.

16
00:02:42,176 --> 00:02:51,549
Now the other side of the product. The same secure sign-in — but choosing 'I am a doctor' opens the practice portal instead.

17
00:02:51,999 --> 00:03:00,952
This is the clinician's Practice Overview — today's schedule, recent patient activity, and the numbers that matter most.

18
00:03:01,402 --> 00:03:09,915
The language choice is app-wide, so the doctor's portal switches too — here is the same practice overview in Telugu.

19
00:03:10,365 --> 00:03:20,238
Appointment requests act as the practice inbox. The doctor accepts or cancels, and the patient is notified inside the app.

20
00:03:20,688 --> 00:03:29,661
The patient roster lists everyone in the practice with their conditions and latest visits. Open any patient for the full picture.

21
00:03:30,111 --> 00:03:37,979
Doctors write prescriptions for a chosen patient, and they're delivered straight into that patient's own medicine list.

22
00:03:38,429 --> 00:03:47,502
Shared reports arrive in the Patient reports inbox. Marking one as seen notifies the patient that their report was reviewed.

23
00:03:47,952 --> 00:04:08,778
That's Health Copilot — a patient app and a doctor portal in one, in English, Hindi and Telugu. All data shown is fictional sample data, and the assistant gives educational information only. Try the live demo, and explore the full source on GitHub. Thanks for watching.
